.TH OXVIF 1 "September 2026" "oxvif-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oxvif \- human- and Agent-friendly ONVIF diagnostic CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oxvif
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oxvif
discovers ONVIF devices, maintains a local secret-free inventory, and runs
read-only diagnostics against one device or a bounded Group/View fleet.
Structured JSON and JSONL output is versioned for automation.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup [TARGET]
Discover interactively when TARGET is omitted, or verify and save TARGET using
a suggested ID plus no-echo credential prompts. Automation supplies --id and
--non-interactive explicitly.
.TP
.B auth DEVICE
Store or replace a device credential in the native operating-system backend.
.TP
.B info [DEVICE]
Display device identity information.
.TP
.B list
List saved IP cameras using local cached identity information. Displays the
current selection, ID, name, address, manufacturer/model, firmware, and serial
number without contacting cameras. The devices command remains compatible;
automation may use device list with structured output.
.TP
.B test [DEVICE]
Run a basic connectivity diagnostic.
.TP
.B health [DEVICE]
Run the comprehensive read-only health suite.
.TP
.B discover
Open a paged, filterable device browser in a human terminal. JSON, redirected,
and non-interactive operation remain deterministic. Interactive scans show
elapsed time, and differential synchronized frames reduce browser flicker.
Enter or the a key explicitly onboards the selected unregistered device using
an inline form with masked password input; Escape returns without saving.
Rows are marked SAVED, NEW, or INCOMPLETE. Use r for saved records, n for
unregistered records, A for all records, and i for a scrollable full-detail
view. The browser's / search and automation's --query option share one
case-insensitive matcher across identity, addressing, registration, types, and
scopes. Automation can pass
--filter registration=saved or --filter registration=unregistered and receives
the same status and saved device ID in structured output.
.TP
.B describe [COMMAND]
Print machine-readable command metadata.
.TP
.B agent guide
Print the versioned Agent contract.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --device " " DEVICE
Select an exact saved device ID.
.TP
.BR --group " " GROUP
Run a supported diagnostic across a saved Group.
.TP
.BR --view " " VIEW
Run a supported diagnostic across a saved View.
.TP
.BR --output " " FORMAT
Select table, JSON, or JSONL output.
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Disable prompts. Use standard input or a trusted process environment for
ephemeral secrets.
.TP
.BR --timeout " " DURATION
Set the per-attempt timeout.
.TP
.BR --retries " " COUNT
Retry transient operations using bounded backoff.
.TP
.BR --ca-certificate " " FILE
Add a PEM trust bundle while retaining certificate-chain and hostname
verification. The option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR -v , " " -vv
Write sanitized diagnostics to standard error. Structured standard output is
unchanged.
.SH CREDENTIALS
Persistent passwords use Windows Credential Manager, macOS Keychain, or Linux
Secret Service. The local registry stores references, never passwords. If a
native backend is unavailable, oxvif returns CREDENTIAL_UNAVAILABLE and does
not create a plaintext fallback. OXVIF_USERNAME and OXVIF_PASSWORD are intended
only for trusted, process-scoped automation.
.SH FILES
The platform configuration directory contains devices.toml and discovery
snapshots. Run
.B oxvif config path
to display resolved locations and
.B oxvif config validate
to validate recovery state.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Stable non-zero categories include invalid input,
missing resources, registry/configuration failure, credential unavailability,
device/network failure, and internal failure. Fleet partial success has its own
documented exit status. Use JSON/JSONL output for the structured error code.
.SH SECURITY
Do not put passwords in command arguments, target URIs, logs, override files,
or version-controlled configuration. There is no insecure TLS bypass.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full manuals and schemas are installed with the package and maintained at
https://github.com/smiti1642/oxvif .
